[size=6][b]𖤝 ReAnimation - third-person - scraps[/b][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/Reanimation3rdpersonOpenMW/main/imgs/Banner.png[/img]

A semi-automated port of some of the ReAnimation v3 1st-person animations to 3rd person. Animations were manually adjusted to fit 3rd person better and were glued with the vanilla/Animation Compilation ones using a smart slop script (also provided), able to add nice-looking procedural upper-body motion based on human biomechanics research.

Covers spears and staves, two-handed swords, hand-to-hand and thrown weapons, for NPCs and for the 3rd-person view. Also includes the third-person one-handed animations from my [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/55059]OpenMW One-handed animations and idle fixes[/url] mod - you don't need to install it, and it will be retired.

As mentioned, this has a good part of a vibe-coded, semi-procedural approach to it. But I would say it turned out quite well after some back and forth, and it does provide great consistency with ReAnimation v3 on those animations that it touches. To be frank, I personally don't care about said consistency so much and can wholeheartedly recommend other completely human-made 3rd-person animation mods, such as [url=https://modding-openmw.com/mods/3rd-person-alt-attacks/]3rd Person Alt Attacks[/url] or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60253]Morrowind Animation Overhaul (MAO)[/url] (Oblivion-ish style animations) or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/58374]Alternative Animation[/url], or anything that might come out in the future. You can also, of course, mix and match by simply removing the .kf files you don't like from the Animations folder of this or any other animation mod made for OpenMW (see Mixing animations below).

Developed for the OpenMW engine. [b]Requires OpenMW 0.51+[/b].

