[size=5][b]𖤝 How to install[/b][/size]

[b]Requires OpenMW 0.51+[/b]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation v3[/url] and its dependency [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/60256]Max Yari's Script Services (MSS)[/url].
[*]Install this mod ([url=https://modding-openmw.com/tips/installing-mods/]this tutorial[/url] explains how) and place it after ReAnimation and your other animation mods in the load order.
[*]Enable [font=Courier New]ReAnimation_ThirdPerson.omwscripts[/font] in the "Content Files" tab of the OpenMW launcher, after [font=Courier New]ReAnimation_API[/font].
[*]OpenMW Launcher -> Settings -> Visuals -> Animations: "Use Additional Animation Sources" and "Smooth Animation Transitions" must be enabled!
[/list]

[size=5][b]𖤝 Recommended mods[/b][/size]

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation v3[/url] - the original first-person animations these were ported from (it's also required, so you already have it).

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/43982]Animation Compilation[/url] - these animations are built on its legs, so the animations this mod doesn't replace match best with it installed.

[size=5][b]𖤝 Mixing animations[/b][/size]

This works only for anims made in the OpenMW format, i.e. the ones that are placed inside the Animations folder. Unfortunately, OpenMW doesn't care about your load order here, since animation file names don't matter: animations aboba.kf and akika.kf can both override the 1h walk cycle, and OpenMW will use the one it loaded last (in alphabetical order). (Load order only matters when two mods have a file with the exact same name - then the later one replaces the other.) This mod's files all start with [font=Courier New]xReAnim3P_[/font], so they load after most others and win.

So, to use different animations from different mods, you will have to go into the mod's Animations folder and delete the .kf files (and .yaml files with the same name, if there are any) corresponding to the anims you don't want to see from this mod - in both [font=Courier New]xbase_anim[/font] and [font=Courier New]xbase_animkna[/font] (the latter is for beast races). You will have to hope that other mods' anims are also split as nicely into separate anim files as this mod's, and you will have to more or less guess which files contain which anims based on their names, since, once again, names don't matter for the engine, so modders are free to name them whatever. In my mods, anim file names usually follow engine animation names loosely. Some names/shorthands that might help you:

[list]
[*]1s = short blades (daggers, shortswords, etc.)
[*]1h = one-handed (1h longswords, 1h maces, 1h axes, etc.)
[*]2w = TwoWide = spears and staves
[*]2c = TwoClose = regular two-handed weapons (claymores, 2h axes, warhammers, etc.)
[*]1t = thrown weapons
[*]hh, h2h = hand-to-hand
[/list]

[size=5][b]𖤝 For Modders and Power Users[/b][/size]

The script itself is slop-magic and allows you to essentially produce a whole, complete set of very passable 3rd-person animations, given a minimum of an idle pose and 3 attack types animated only on the upper body. The script just magically matches it up with 3rd-person legs and procedurally generates locomotion animations based on the idle pose that look... maybe not absolutely great, but certainly better than the original animations. So if you are planning to, say, make a novel weapon class but don't want to deal with all the dozens of animations that need to be made for running, walking, strafing, etc., you can avoid doing all of that completely.

You can also use the same script to make a 3rd-person version of any 1st-person anims that you like, such as MCAR, MAGIC, or anything else. You merely need Python to run it. It has many different tweakable parameters, with descriptions of those built into the interactive part of the script, but most likely you can just run it using the default settings and get a good output.

The script comes with ReAnimation: [font=Courier New]Sources/Tools/FirstToThird/first_to_third.py[/font] in its archive or [url=https://github.com/MaxYari/OpenMWReAnimation/tree/main/Sources/Tools/FirstToThird]git repository[/url] (keep the [font=Courier New]FBACompat[/font] folder next to it; the script uses it). Run it without arguments to go through the settings one by one. This set was built from ReAnimation's folder with:

[code]python3 Sources/Tools/FirstToThird/first_to_third.py -y \
  --first "../ReAnimation Scraps 3rd Person/Animations/1st person sources" \
  --third "../Animation Compilation 0.40-43982-0-40/Animation Compilation" \
  --legs-from "2hstaffspearguard=idle2w@start, 2hstaffspearrecoil=idle2w@start" \
  --prefix "xReAnim3P_"[/code]

